## Summary

**What changed:** `src/tool_wrappers.rs`

**Edit 1 — `targeted_recovery_hint` match arms (line 1026):** Added 5 new exit code arms before the wildcard `_ => ""`:

| Code | Signal | Hint |
|------|--------|------|
| 130 | SIGINT | Interrupted — try longer timeout or smaller scope |
| 137 | SIGKILL | OOM — reduce input size or use memory-efficient command |
| 139 | SIGSEGV | Tool crashed — try different tool or check for known bugs |
| 141 | SIGPIPE | Pipe closed early — use bounded command (head -n, tail -n) |
| 143 | SIGTERM | Terminated — retry once, then escalate |

**Edit 2 — New test `test_targeted_recovery_hint_bash_signal_exit_codes`:** Tests that each of the 5 signal-kill exit codes (130, 137, 139, 141, 143) returns a non-empty hint containing the signal name and appropriate context keywords (interrupted, memory, crashed, pipe/bounded, terminated).

**Verification:**
• `cargo test tool_wrappers`: 119 tests passed (including 6 new assertions)
• `cargo fmt -- --check`: passed
• `cargo check`: passed

**Expected Evidence satisfied:** Signal-kill exit codes now produce meaningful recovery hints instead of empty strings, reducing retry cycles for common pipeline failures like SIGPIPE (141).

